README.OSK -- VT-100 terminal program for the MM/1Brian Marcotte's VT-100, "a very simple temulator for OS-9", converted toOS-9/68000 and K-Windows by Brian C. White (June 1993, GCC 1.43).CMDS/MM1/vt100 is the archive's own binary; vt is the archive's exampleprocedure file, which sets the palette with `display' and starts vt100 on/t4 in a new window.Changes: none.Not tested: it needs an MM/1's K-Windows display and a serial port.